        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-1333",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Quadratic ReDoS in the `<system>` prompt-injection pattern: `<\\s*\\/?\\s*` backtracks O(n^2) on a whitespace run after `<`.\n\ncheckContent is the module explicitly designed to receive hostile documents (signage, emails, wayfinding docs) and runs every PROMPT_INJECTION_PATTERNS regex over the whole folded document (up to 200,000 chars). Pattern index 6, `/<\\s*\\/?\\s*(?:system|assistant|instructions?)\\s*>/iu`, has two `\\s*` quantifiers separated only by an optional `\\/?`; on `<` followed by a long whitespace run and no keyword, the engine tries every split of the run between the two `\\s*` (about N^2/2 steps).\n\nImpact: CPU exhaustion / hang of the process calling checkContent; per-request denial of service for any long-running wrapper. No confidentiality or integrity impact.\n\nExploit scenario: An attacker crafts a document starting with `<` followed by ~199,998 spaces and a letter such as `x` (under both the 200,000-char and 2 MB limits) and gets the victim to audit it with `wayfinding-audit check <file>` or the /wayfinding-content-check command. The direction-word, north-up and you-are-here passes finish quickly, then the loop at line 157 reaches pattern 6: at position 0 the first `\\s*` takes all spaces, the keyword fails on `x`, and the engine backtracks through every (k, N-k) split of the whitespace run, roughly 2e10 steps, before giving up. The CLI or the agent invoking it hangs for tens of seconds to minutes. Timing was not measured here; the estimate follows from the backtracking structure.\n\nPreconditions: Attacker controls the content passed to checkContent (the documented input is third-party documents); Content contains `<` followed by a long whitespace run that is not followed by system/assistant/instruction(s).\n\nRecommendation: Remove the ambiguity: use a single optional-whitespace group, e.g. `/<\\s*(?:\\/\\s*)?(?:system|assistant|instructions?)\\s*>/iu`, or bound whitespace with `\\s{0,8}` on each side. Extend the test-security.ts ReDoS suite with a `<` + long-whitespace case and with a static check for adjacent or quantifier-only-separated `\\s*`/`\\s+` atoms.\n\nCWE-1333. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "lib/content-check.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 158,
                  "snippet": {
