          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F4",
              "title": "Quadratic ReDoS in the `<system>` prompt-injection pattern: `<\\s*\\/?\\s*` backtracks O(n^2) on a whitespace run after `<`",
              "impact": "CPU exhaustion / hang of the process calling checkContent; per-request denial of service for any long-running wrapper. No confidentiality or integrity impact.",
              "file": "lib/content-check.ts",
              "line": 158,
              "description": "checkContent is the module explicitly designed to receive hostile documents (signage, emails, wayfinding docs) and runs every PROMPT_INJECTION_PATTERNS regex over the whole folded document (up to 200,000 chars). Pattern index 6, `/<\\s*\\/?\\s*(?:system|assistant|instructions?)\\s*>/iu`, has two `\\s*` quantifiers separated only by an optional `\\/?`; on `<` followed by a long whitespace run and no keyword, the engine tries every split of the run between the two `\\s*` (about N^2/2 steps).",
              "exploit_scenario": "An attacker crafts a document starting with `<` followed by ~199,998 spaces and a letter such as `x` (under both the 200,000-char and 2 MB limits) and gets the victim to audit it with `wayfinding-audit check <file>` or the /wayfinding-content-check command. The direction-word, north-up and you-are-here passes finish quickly, then the loop at line 157 reaches pattern 6: at position 0 the first `\\s*` takes all spaces, the keyword fails on `x`, and the engine backtracks through every (k, N-k) split of the whitespace run, roughly 2e10 steps, before giving up. The CLI or the agent invoking it hangs for tens of seconds to minutes. Timing was not measured here; the estimate follows from the backtracking structure.",
              "preconditions": [
                "Attacker controls the content passed to checkContent (the documented input is third-party documents)",
                "Content contains `<` followed by a long whitespace run that is not followed by system/assistant/instruction(s)"
              ],
              "category": "Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity",
              "severity": "LOW",
              "confidence": "high",
              "recommendation": "Remove the ambiguity: use a single optional-whitespace group, e.g. `/<\\s*(?:\\/\\s*)?(?:system|assistant|instructions?)\\s*>/iu`, or bound whitespace with `\\s{0,8}` on each side. Extend the test-security.ts ReDoS suite with a `<` + long-whitespace case and with a static check for adjacent or quantifier-only-separated `\\s*`/`\\s+` atoms.",
              "cwe_id": "CWE-1333",
              "snippet": "    const m = re.exec(folded);",
              "symbol": "checkContent",
              "declared_line": 158,
              "claudeSecurityPluginFindingId": "v3:c2e42c0b26950e31fc1a8d03e6a7c5af627adddbfc1efe55f734faac05d54f37",
              "verification": {
                "panel": {
                  "true": 3,
                  "false": 0,
                  "voters": 3
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "uncategorized",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Direction-word replacement uses offsets from the folded string but slices the NFC string, so Unicode input that changes length under NFD leaves direction words in the output.\n\nfind_direction_words() computes match offsets on fold(NFC(text)) (NFD, strip Mn, lower), but rewrite() applies those offsets to unicodedata.normalize('NFC', step). Any character whose canonical decomposition contains non-Mn code points (Hangul syllables -> 2-3 Jamo of category Lo; several Indic Mc vowel signs) makes the folded string longer than the NFC string, so the slice at line 137 lands at the wrong place, the lateral direction word survives, and the tool still reports 'side bound to body anchor'.\n\nImpact: Integrity of the safety transformation: lateral direction words survive the rewrite in the anchor-binding branch and the output is garbled, while notes assert success. Bounded: the lexicon filter is also evadable by synonyms or zero-width characters, so this is a reliability gap in a non-comprehensive filter rather than a boundary crossing.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker-authored directions (the threat model treats pasted directions as hostile) contain a step such as '한국 Turn left.' with an anchor supplied and no landmark for that step. NFC length is 13; folded length is 17 because each Hangul syllable decomposes to Jamo that are not stripped. The hit for 'left' is recorded at folded index 12-16; rebuilt[:12] is '한국 Turn left' and rebuilt[16:] is empty, producing '한국 Turn lefttoward your watch side' while the note claims the side was bound. The word the tool exists to remove reaches the DTD reader unchanged, with no diagnostic.\n\nPreconditions: rewrite() called with an anchor and fewer landmarks than steps (the `elif lateral and anchor` branch); step text contains characters whose NFD decomposition includes non-Mn code points (Hangul syllables, some Indic Mc vowel signs).\n\nRecommendation: Build `rebuilt` from the same folded string the offsets were computed on, or compute hits on the NFC string directly (fold per character while keeping an offset map from folded index back to NFC index), and after rebuilding re-run find_direction_words on the result and raise/flag if any lateral hit remains.\n\nCWE-176. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "samples/rewrite_directions.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 137,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "                rebuilt = rebuilt[:h[\"index\"]] + phrase + rebuilt[h[\"end\"]:]"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "rewrite",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "rewrite"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
